"Every claim and every picture is verified against the ESV (esv.org, Bible Gateway and Biblia) by an independent fact-checker, over six rounds; 23 rows, none pending. Quotes in the third column are exact ESV wording.\n\n| Claim | Verse | ESV wording it rests on | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Most people credit the hair, and Samson himself tied his strength to it | [Judges 16:17](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:17/) | \"If my head is shaved, then my strength will leave me\" | Verified |\n| Three times the Spirit of the LORD rushed upon him, the only three in Judges | [Judges 14:6, 14:19, 15:14](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+14:6/) | \"the Spirit of the LORD rushed upon him\" | Verified, exact |\n| His weakness was his eyes | [Judges 14:1, 14:7, 16:1](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+14:1/) | \"saw\" \u00b7 \"she was right in Samson's eyes\" \u00b7 \"he saw a prostitute\" | Verified |\n| He demanded a wife from Israel's enemies | [Judges 13:1, 14:1\u20134](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+14:1-4/) | \"the LORD gave them into the hand of the Philistines for forty years\" \u00b7 \"Get her for me, for she is right in my eyes.\" | Verified, quote exact |\n| Later, he told Delilah he was set apart to God. No razor, or his strength would leave | [Judges 13:5, 16:4, 16:17](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:4-17/) | \"a Nazirite to God from my mother's womb\" \u00b7 \"After this he loved a woman in the Valley of Sorek, whose name was Delilah\" \u00b7 \"If my head is shaved, then my strength will leave me\" | Verified (paraphrase; reworded in round 6, since Judges never calls it a vow) |\n| She had his seven locks shaved; the LORD had left him | [Judges 16:19\u201320](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:19-20/) | \"had him shave off the seven locks of his head\" \u00b7 \"he did not know that the LORD had left him\" | Verified |\n| The man who lived by his eyes lost his eyes | [Judges 14:3, 16:21](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:21/) | \"gouged out his eyes\" | Verified |\n| Blind, he looked to God for strength, to avenge his two eyes | [Judges 16:28](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:28/) | \"Then Samson called to the LORD\" \u00b7 \"please strengthen me only this once, O God, that I may be avenged on the Philistines for my two eyes\" | Verified |\n| And the house fell | [Judges 16:30](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:30/) | \"he bowed with all his strength, and the house fell\" | Verified |\n| Hebrews 11 names him in a list. Through faith they \"were made strong out of weakness\" | [Hebrews 11:32\u201334](https://www.esv.org/verses/Hebrews+11:32-34/) | \"Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, of David and Samuel and the prophets\" \u00b7 \"who through faith\" \u00b7 \"were made strong out of weakness\" | Verified, quote exact (reworded in round 5 so it covers the whole list, not the collapse) |\n| Verdict: a flawed hero of faith; his failures his own, his strength God's | [Judges 16:1, 16:17, 16:20, 16:28; Hebrews 11:32\u201333, 11:39](https://www.esv.org/verses/Hebrews+11:32-39/) | \"who through faith conquered kingdoms\" \u00b7 \"commended through their faith\" | Verified |\n| Picture: the lion charges first; he tears it apart bare-handed | [Judges 14:5\u20136](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+14:5-6/) | \"a young lion came toward him roaring\" \u00b7 \"although he had nothing in his hand, he tore the lion in pieces\" | Verified |\n| Picture: the ropes fall away, with no fire on him | [Judges 15:14](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+15:14/) | \"became as flax that has caught fire, and his bonds melted off his hands\" | Verified (a simile) |\n| Picture: \"Get her for me\" is said at home in Zorah, with no woman there | [Judges 13:2, 14:1\u20133](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+14:1-3/) | \"came up and told his father and mother\" | Verified (corrected in round 1) |\n| Picture: the woman at Timnah is lit naturally, not as a villain | [Judges 14:4](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+14:4/) | \"it was from the LORD, for he was seeking an opportunity against the Philistines\" | Verified |\n| Picture: a faint gold stays through his failures and fades after the shave while he sleeps; he wakes and tries to shake himself free | [Judges 16:3, 16:19\u201320](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:19-20/) | \"his strength left him\" \u00b7 \"shake myself free\" | Verified (corrected in round 4) |\n| Picture: his hair is growing back by the house scene | [Judges 16:22](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:22/) | \"the hair of his head began to grow again\" | Verified |\n| Picture: the house scene, with about 3,000 on the roof and praise when they see him | [Judges 16:23\u201327](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:23-27/) | \"to rejoice\" \u00b7 \"when the people saw him, they praised their god\" \u00b7 \"on the roof there were about 3,000 men and women\" | Verified (corrected in round 4) |\n| Picture: led by the hand; he only feels the pillars while he prays and grips them after | [Judges 16:26\u201329](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:26-29/) | \"the young man who held him by the hand\" \u00b7 \"his right hand on the one and his left hand on the other\" | Verified (corrected in round 4) |\n| Picture: his family lays him in his father's tomb, away from the ruins; dawn in natural light, not the Spirit's gold | [Judges 16:31](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:31/) | \"his brothers and all his family came down and took him\u2026 buried him between Zorah and Eshtaol in the tomb of Manoah his father\" | Verified |\n| Caption: before he was born, the angel of the LORD said he would \"begin to save Israel from the hand of the Philistines\" | [Judges 13:3\u20135](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+13:3-5/) | \"the angel of the LORD appeared to the woman\" \u00b7 \"and he shall begin to save Israel from the hand of the Philistines\" | Verified, exact (corrected in round 5) |\n| Caption: the crowd was praising their god Dagon for handing Samson over | [Judges 16:23\u201324](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+16:23-24/) | \"Our god has given Samson our enemy into our hand\" \u00b7 \"they praised their god\" | Verified |\n| Caption: the last verse of Judges echoes his words | [Judges 14:3, 21:25](https://www.esv.org/verses/Judges+21:25/) | \"Everyone did what was right in his own eyes.\" | Verified, exact |\n"
